---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { SOURCE_URL } from "../data/site";
import { manifest } from "../data/screenshots";
import { formatDate } from "../lib/release";
import { photos, PHOTOS_CHECKED } from "../data/photos";

const app = [
  {
    name: "MediaPipe Tasks Vision, including its WebAssembly runtime",
    detail: "@mediapipe/tasks-vision 0.10.35, by Google",
    license: "Apache License 2.0",
  },
  {
    name: "MediaPipe Face Landmarker model",
    detail: "face_landmarker.task, float16, version 1, by Google",
    license: "Apache License 2.0",
  },
  {
    name: "RealEye's open-source eye-image model",
    detail: "Reads where you look from small eye images, on the device",
    license: "See THIRD_PARTY.md",
  },
  {
    name: "Synapse-Mesh and the AGENCY desktop design",
    detail:
      "By Ray: the request router with its Cisco network sentinel, and the macOS-style desktop interface",
    license: "Part of this project",
  },
  {
    name: "QR Code Generator for JavaScript",
    detail: "qrcode-generator 1.4.4, by Kazuhiko Arase",
    license: "MIT License",
  },
  {
    name: "Atkinson Hyperlegible",
    detail: "Typeface by the Braille Institute of America, packaged by Fontsource",
    license: "SIL Open Font License 1.1",
  },
  {
    name: "React, Vite, FastAPI, Pydantic, Uvicorn, the Google Gen AI SDK and other dependencies",
    detail: "Listed in the project's package.json and backend requirements files",
    license: "Their own open-source licenses",
  },
];

const site = [
  { name: "Astro", detail: "The tool that builds this site into plain HTML", license: "MIT License" },
  {
    name: "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next",
    detail:
      "The text face. Typeface by the Braille Institute of America; @fontsource-variable/atkinson-hyperlegible-next 5.3.0, served from this site",
    license: "SIL Open Font License 1.1",
  },
  {
    name: "Fraunces",
    detail:
      "The headline face. Typeface by Undercase Type (Phaedra Charles and Flavia Zimbardi); @fontsource-variable/fraunces 5.3.0, served from this site",
    license: "SIL Open Font License 1.1",
  },
  { name: "sharp", detail: "Image resizing at build time", license: "Apache License 2.0" },
  {
    name: "Playwright, axe-core, Lighthouse CI, Vitest, TypeScript, Prettier",
    detail: "Testing and checking tools, used only when building; none of them run in your browser",
    license: "Apache License 2.0, MPL 2.0 (axe-core) and MIT",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Credits and licenses: AGENCY"
  description="The open-source work and the photographs AGENCY and this website use, with their authors and licenses."
  current="credits"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Credits and licenses"
    title="Built on the work of others"
    lede="AGENCY and this site use these components and photographs. Thank you to everyone who made them."
  />
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h2 id="app">In the AGENCY app</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Components in the AGENCY app" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Component</th>
            <th scope="col">Details</th>
            <th scope="col">License</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {app.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{c.name}</th>
              <td>{c.detail}</td>
              <td>{c.license}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The authoritative list, with versions and checksums, is{" "}
      <a href={`${SOURCE_URL}/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY.md`}>THIRD_PARTY.md</a> in the repository. It grows as
      AGENCY adds parts such as the Mac app shell and the Chrome extension.
    </p>

    <h2 id="site">In this website</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Components in this website" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Component</th>
            <th scope="col">Details</th>
            <th scope="col">License</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{c.name}</th>
              <td>{c.detail}</td>
              <td>{c.license}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="photos">Photographs</h2>
    <p>
      The photographs of people on this site are freely licensed.{" "}
      <strong>The people in them are not AGENCY users</strong> and have no connection to the project; we use
      the photos to show who we build for. Each one was resized and converted to modern image formats for the
      web; some are also cropped on screen to fit their frame. Checked on {formatDate(PHOTOS_CHECKED)}. A
      machine-readable list is in the repository at <code>site/src/data/photos.json</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Photographs and their licenses" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Photo</th>
            <th scope="col">Author</th>
            <th scope="col">License</th>
            <th scope="col">Changes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {photos.map((p) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                <a href={p.source}>{p.title}</a>
                <span class="credit-alt">{p.alt}</span>
              </th>
              <td>{p.authorUrl ? <a href={p.authorUrl}>{p.author}</a> : p.author}</td>
              <td>
                <a href={p.licenseUrl}>{p.license}</a>
              </td>
              <td>{p.changes}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="screenshots">Screenshots</h2>
    <p>
      Every screenshot on this site is a real capture of the AGENCY app, taken automatically by a script in
      the repository (<code>site/scripts/capture-screenshots.mjs</code>) on {manifest.captured} from commit{" "}
      <code>{manifest.commit}</code>, using fictional demo data (“Jordan”, “Thai Basil” and practice services)
      and the built-in demo agent. None are mock-ups.
    </p>
    <p>
      The three large stills on the home page are single frames of the demo video, which was recorded on the
      real app with live Gemini and practice services. No webcam was on the recording machine, so a scripted
      pointer stands in for the eyes; the yellow rings in them are the app's own dwell rings. The “Try it
      here” phrases, the full stop in the headline and the network-mode bars on Inside AGENCY are drawn for
      this site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Bartlett G, Blais R, Tamblyn R, Clermont RJ, MacGibbon B.{" "}
        <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2396356">
          Impact of patient communication problems on the risk of preventable adverse events in acute care
          settings
        </a>
        . CMAJ 2008;178(12):1555–62.
      </li>
      <li>
        Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC): about 33,000 people in the United States live with
        ALS.
      </li>
      <li>
        Beukelman D, Fager S, Nordness A. Communication support for people with ALS. Neurology Research
        International, 2011: 80 to 95% of people with ALS become unable to rely on natural speech.
      </li>
      <li>
        Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services (CMS), 2026 DMEPOS fee schedule: about $9,646 for a
        speech-generating device.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="project">AGENCY itself</h2>
    <p>
      AGENCY is made by Neil Gilani, Rayansh “Ray” Bakshi and Ryan Cho. It won 1st place in the Cloud AI track
      at the UCSC AI Hackathon, and is built in the open on <a href={SOURCE_URL}>GitHub</a>. The project
      hasn't chosen a license for its own code yet; until it does, the code can be read but no license to
      reuse it is granted.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .credit-alt {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
